<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<UserControl
    x:Class="Phoenix.Controls.Hub.WinUI.Panels.CountersPanel.CountersView"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:local="using:Phoenix.Controls.Hub.WinUI.Panels.CountersPanel"
    xmlns:cmn="using:Phoenix.Controls.Hub.WinUI.Panels.Common"
    xmlns:loc="using:Phoenix.Controls.Hub.WinUI.Localization"
    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
    VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
    HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch"
    VerticalContentAlignment="Stretch"
    AutomationProperties.Name="Counters page"
    AutomationProperties.HelpText="Named tally counters: pick one from the roster on the right to edit its chat command, roles and step, and to set, reset or step its live count."
    loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.page.a11y"
    loc:Localize.HelpTextKey="panel.counters.page.help">

    <!--
        ══════════════════ THE HOUSE TOOL-PAGE SHELL ══════════════════

        Row 0  ToolPageHeader — the 48 px band: name · master switch · ONE state
               phrase · the page's single brass CTA. It replaces THREE rows this
               page used to stack: the action strip, the status pill inside it,
               and the pinned master-state banner at the top of the left column.
               All three rendered the same boolean in three vocabularies
               (DISABLED / dormant / "no chat command…") and cost ~94 px before a
               setting was visible.
        Row 1  two-column body: the detail column takes the star, the live column
               is a FIXED 300 px. No ColumnSpacing — the right column's left
               border IS the divider.

               LEFT  *    the SELECTED counter's detail scroller. Its first child
                          is now the LIVE COUNT card: the stat strip that used to
                          head it (COUNTERS / ACTIVE / TOTAL COUNT) is gone. Two
                          of those three read 0 on a fresh install, and the one
                          worth a glance — how many counters exist — is already
                          in the live column's own header (RosterCountText).
               RIGHT 300  the tool-wide roster and the source note.

        WHERE THE ACTIVITY FEED WENT. Removed. It is a watch surface: what a
        counter did 40 seconds ago does not help someone editing a step size or a
        role gate, and it was the tallest thing in a 300 px column. The session
        ring behind it (CountersService's RecordActivity → ToolActivityRing) is
        untouched and still records; only this page's rendering of it is gone.

        NO IsEnabled GATE ON THE COUNT CONTROLS, and that is deliberate. The
        house shell gates the detail scroller on the master switch; Counters must
        not. Its count controls (− / + / RESET / SET) are documented as working
        while the tool is dormant — the databank stays writable and the numbers
        keep moving — so greying them would be a behaviour regression dressed up
        as a layout change. The header's state phrase says so in three words
        instead of a paragraph: "off · databank writable".

        NO ENTRANCE ANIMATION. the Pre-Builds rail already runs FadeSlideIn on every tool
        activation; the page-side entrance this file used to run was the second
        of two.
    -->

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <!-- KEPT, checked type by type: after the conversions below this
                     page still declares TextBox (name, step, cooldown, command,
                     reply template, set-value). It declares no ComboBox, no
                     ToggleSwitch, no CheckBox and no Pivot — the six checkboxes
                     visible in the roles card belong to RoleCheckRow, and the
                     master ToggleSwitch belongs to ToolPageHeader; both merge
                     this same dictionary themselves. -->
                <ResourceDictionary Source="ms-appx:///Panels/Common/ToolControlStyles.xaml" />
                <!-- Keyed-only shell styles. Never merged into App.xaml. -->
                <ResourceDictionary Source="ms-appx:///Panels/Common/ToolShellStyles.xaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <Grid Background="{StaticResource CoalSurfaceBrush}">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- ══════════════════ ROW 0 — HEADER BAND ══════════════════
             Title, master switch, state phrase and the ONE brass CTA are all set
             from code-behind (ToolPageHeader is deliberately plain properties,
             not DPs). The master flip still routes through ViewModel.MasterEnabled
             → SaveNow, so it keeps bypassing the 400 ms debounce exactly as the
             old chip did.

             DELETE COUNTER is NOT here. The band has no danger slot, and the verb
             was never tool-wide to begin with: it acts on the SELECTED counter.
             It now sits at the foot of that counter's own detail column, which is
             the surface it destroys. -->
        <cmn:ToolPageHeader Grid.Row="0" x:Name="PageHeader" />

        <!-- ══════════════════ ROW 1 — TWO-COLUMN BODY ══════════════════ -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="1">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="300" />
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

            <!-- ───────────── LEFT * : the selected counter ─────────────
                 One cell, two overlaid siblings: the detail scroller and its
                 empty state. The pinned master-state band that used to sit above
                 them is gone — its sentence is the header band's state phrase
                 now, and its consequence half ("the open Counters table still
                 answers db.* nodes") survives verbatim in the source note under
                 the roster, which is where the streamer is already looking when
                 that question comes up. -->
            <Grid Grid.Column="0">

                <!-- The detail pane's VISIBILITY is bound; its content is never
                     swapped or virtualized, so a focused TextBox stays in the
                     tree and commits its LostFocus edit before a roster click
                     changes the selection. -->
                <ScrollViewer x:Name="DetailScroll"
                              Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.DetailVisibility, Mode=OneWay}"
                              VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                              HorizontalScrollMode="Disabled">
                    <StackPanel Spacing="12" Padding="14">

                        <!-- ── LIVE COUNT ─────────────────────────────────
                             The scroller's FIRST child now. The three stat
                             tiles that used to head it (COUNTERS / ACTIVE /
                             TOTAL COUNT) are gone: on a fresh install two of
                             them read 0, and the third — how many counters
                             exist — is already the live column's header
                             value. A config surface does not open with a
                             dashboard.

                             THIS number stays, and is not a stat tile: it is
                             the value the four buttons beside it edit.
                             NOT gated on the master switch, by design: these
                             controls keep working while the tool is dormant,
                             because the databank does. -->
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource ToolSectionCardStyle}">
                            <Grid ColumnSpacing="12">
                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="2">
                                    <TextBlock Text="LIVE COUNT" Style="{StaticResource ToolEyebrowTextStyle}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.live.eyebrow" />
                                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.CountText, Mode=OneWay}"
                                               FontFamily="{StaticResource DisplayFont}"
                                               FontSize="26" CharacterSpacing="20"
                                               Foreground="{StaticResource CoalPaperBrush}"
                                               MinWidth="64"
                                               AutomationProperties.LiveSetting="Polite" />
                                </StackPanel>

                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                                            VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <Button Style="{StaticResource ToolSecondaryButtonStyle}"
                                            MinWidth="36" Padding="0"
                                            Click="OnStepDownClick"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Step count down"
                                            loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.live.step_down.a11y">
                                        <TextBlock Text="&#x2212;" Style="{StaticResource ToolStripLabelTextStyle}"
                                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                                    </Button>
                                    <Button Style="{StaticResource ToolSecondaryButtonStyle}"
                                            MinWidth="36" Padding="0"
                                            Click="OnStepUpClick"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Step count up"
                                            loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.live.step_up.a11y">
                                        <TextBlock Text="+" Style="{StaticResource ToolStripLabelTextStyle}"
                                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                                    </Button>
                                    <Button Style="{StaticResource ToolSecondaryButtonStyle}"
                                            Click="OnResetClick"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Reset count to zero"
                                            loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.live.reset.a11y">
                                        <TextBlock Text="RESET" Style="{StaticResource ToolStripLabelTextStyle}"
                                                   loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.live.reset.label" />
                                    </Button>
                                    <TextBox Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.SetValueText, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             Width="80" PlaceholderText="0"
                                             FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="11"
                                             TextAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="Value to set"
                                             loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.live.set_value.a11y" />
                                    <!-- Neutral, like its three neighbours. The page's
                                         one brass CTA is + ADD COUNTER in the header
                                         band; a brass button mid-card would read as the
                                         page's primary action when it is one of four
                                         equal count controls. -->
                                    <Button Style="{StaticResource ToolSecondaryButtonStyle}"
                                            Click="OnSetClick"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Set count to the value on the left"
                                            loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.live.set.a11y">
                                        <TextBlock Text="SET" Style="{StaticResource ToolStripLabelTextStyle}"
                                                   loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.live.set.label" />
                                    </Button>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>

                        <!-- ── CHAT COMMANDS ──────────────────────────────
                             ★ The five shapes one counter answers to. Four of
                             them exist in no field on this page: the parser mints
                             !deaths+ / !deaths- / !setdeaths / !resetdeaths by
                             concatenation off the single command word below.

                             The page was not silent about them — the
                             EffectiveCommandHint line inside the settings card
                             lists the five words, and the ROLES card names its
                             two gates "WHO CAN VIEW" and "WHO CAN MODIFY
                             (+/-/SET/RESET)". What no surface did was put the two
                             together: which of those five words each gate governs
                             is something the streamer had to reassemble from the
                             parenthesis in a header. Here every word carries its
                             own gate on its own row, and its own dimming when the
                             counter's chat toggle is off.

                             SCOPED TO THE SELECTED COUNTER, which is why it sits
                             in this column at all — see ChatCommands on the
                             ViewModel for why a tool-wide rendering (five rows
                             per counter) does not belong over a per-counter
                             editor. It re-renders as the name, the command word,
                             the roles and the chat toggle below are edited.

                             BELOW LIVE COUNT, ABOVE the fields. Below, because
                             the count readout and its four buttons are the one
                             thing on this page a streamer touches mid-stream and
                             they stay the first card in the scroller. Above,
                             because this is the ANSWER the card underneath is
                             configuring, and an answer printed after its inputs
                             reads as a footnote. -->
                        <cmn:ToolCommandList Commands="{x:Bind ViewModel.ChatCommands, Mode=OneWay}"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="Chat commands for the selected counter"
                                             loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.commands.a11y" />

                        <!-- ── SETTINGS ─────────────────────────────────── -->
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource ToolSectionCardStyle}">
                            <StackPanel Spacing="10">
                                <TextBlock Text="COUNTER" Style="{StaticResource ToolEyebrowTextStyle}"
                                           loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.eyebrow" />

                                <Grid ColumnSpacing="10">
                                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="150" />
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Name"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolSettingsLabelTextStyle}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.name.label" />
                                    <TextBox Grid.Column="1"
                                             Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.Name, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             PlaceholderText="deaths"
                                             HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                             Width="320"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="Counter name"
                                             loc:Localize.PlaceholderKey="panel.counters.settings.name.placeholder"
                                             loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.settings.name.a11y" />
                                </Grid>

                                <Grid ColumnSpacing="10">
                                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="150" />
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Floor at zero"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolSettingsLabelTextStyle}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.floor.label" />
                                    <!-- CheckBox → TogglePill in a borderless Button host.
                                         The Button owns the Click and the accessible name;
                                         the pill is display-only. -->
                                    <Button Grid.Column="1"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                            Padding="0,4,10,4"
                                            Background="Transparent"
                                            BorderThickness="0"
                                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource Radius1Corner}"
                                            Click="OnFloorAtZeroClick"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Floor this counter at zero"
                                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Never let this counter go below 0."
                                            loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.settings.floor.a11y"
                                            loc:Localize.TooltipKey="panel.counters.settings.floor.tip">
                                        <cmn:TogglePill IsOn="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.FloorAtZero, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                        Label="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.FloorAtZeroLabel, Mode=OneWay}" />
                                    </Button>
                                </Grid>

                                <Grid ColumnSpacing="10">
                                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="150" />
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Step"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolSettingsLabelTextStyle}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.step.label" />
                                    <TextBox Grid.Column="1"
                                             Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.StepText, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             Width="80"
                                             FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="11"
                                             TextAlignment="Right"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="Step size"
                                             loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.settings.step.a11y" />
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="how far &#x2212; and + move it"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.step.hint" />
                                </Grid>

                                <Grid ColumnSpacing="10">
                                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="150" />
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Cooldown (s)"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolSettingsLabelTextStyle}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.cooldown.label" />
                                    <TextBox Grid.Column="1"
                                             Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.CooldownText, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             Width="80"
                                             FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="11"
                                             TextAlignment="Right"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="Chat command cooldown in seconds"
                                             loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.settings.cooldown.a11y" />
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="per-viewer wait between chat uses"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.cooldown.hint" />
                                </Grid>

                                <Border Height="1" Background="{StaticResource CoalRaisedBrush}" />

                                <Grid ColumnSpacing="10">
                                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="150" />
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Chat command"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolSettingsLabelTextStyle}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.command.label" />
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="12"
                                                VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <Button Padding="0,4,10,4"
                                                Background="Transparent"
                                                BorderThickness="0"
                                                CornerRadius="{StaticResource Radius1Corner}"
                                                Click="OnChatEnabledClick"
                                                AutomationProperties.Name="Answer this counter in chat"
                                                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.settings.chat_enabled.a11y">
                                            <cmn:TogglePill IsOn="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.ChatEnabled, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                            Label="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.ChatEnabledLabel, Mode=OneWay}" />
                                        </Button>
                                        <TextBlock Text="!" Style="{StaticResource ToolSettingsLabelTextStyle}" />
                                        <TextBox Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.Command, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                 PlaceholderText="defaults to Name" Width="180"
                                                 FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="11"
                                                 VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                 AutomationProperties.Name="Chat command word"
                                                 loc:Localize.PlaceholderKey="panel.counters.settings.command.placeholder"
                                                 loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.settings.command.a11y" />
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Grid>

                                <!-- The Command → Name fallback, resolved: the
                                     word the parser will really match, echoed
                                     beside the field that sets it. The CHAT
                                     COMMANDS block above now spells the five
                                     shapes out per gate, so this line is no
                                     longer the page's only enumeration of them —
                                     it stays for the one thing that block cannot
                                     say. A counter with neither a command word
                                     nor a name mints NO rows at all, so the
                                     block goes quietly empty while this line
                                     says "(name a counter)", which is the
                                     actionable half. -->
                                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.EffectiveCommandHint, Mode=OneWay}"
                                           Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}" />

                                <Border Height="1" Background="{StaticResource CoalRaisedBrush}" />

                                <StackPanel Spacing="3">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Reply template &#xB7; {name} / {count} &#xB7; empty = default"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.settings.reply.label" />
                                    <TextBox Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.ReplyTemplate, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             PlaceholderText="{}{name} count: {count}"
                                             HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="Chat reply template"
                                             loc:Localize.PlaceholderKey="panel.counters.settings.reply.placeholder"
                                             loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.settings.reply.a11y" />
                                </StackPanel>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Border>

                        <!-- ── ROLES ────────────────────────────────────────
                             Stacked vertically, one gate per full-width row.
                             RoleCheckRow lays out in WrapRowPanel, which needs
                             a finite-width measure host to fold instead of
                             clipping: a vertical StackPanel inside a STAR-width
                             card is that host. Never put one in an Auto column
                             or a horizontal StackPanel. -->
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource ToolSectionCardStyle}">
                            <StackPanel Spacing="10">
                                <TextBlock Text="WHO CAN USE IT" Style="{StaticResource ToolEyebrowTextStyle}"
                                           loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roles.eyebrow" />
                                <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                                    <TextBlock Text="WHO CAN VIEW"
                                               FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}"
                                               FontSize="10" CharacterSpacing="120"
                                               Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roles.view.label" />
                                    <cmn:RoleCheckRow Roles="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.ViewRoles, Mode=OneWay}" />
                                </StackPanel>
                                <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                                    <TextBlock Text="WHO CAN MODIFY (+/-/SET/RESET)"
                                               FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}"
                                               FontSize="10" CharacterSpacing="120"
                                               Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roles.modify.label" />
                                    <cmn:RoleCheckRow Roles="{x:Bind ViewModel.SelectedCounter.ModifyRoles, Mode=OneWay}" />
                                </StackPanel>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Border>

                        <!-- ── DELETE ───────────────────────────────────────
                             Re-homed from the old action strip, unchanged in
                             chrome, handler, tooltip and accessible name. It
                             belongs here: it destroys the SELECTED counter,
                             so it sits at the foot of that counter's own
                             column rather than in a tool-wide band. The
                             HasSelection gate is kept as-is — the scroller is
                             already collapsed without a selection, so the
                             binding is now belt-and-braces rather than the
                             only guard, and removing it would be a behaviour
                             change for no gain. -->
                        <Button x:Name="DeleteCounterButton"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                Style="{StaticResource ToolDangerButtonStyle}"
                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.HasSelection, Mode=OneWay}"
                                Click="OnDeleteCounterClick"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Delete the selected counter"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Removes the counter and drops its row from the open Counters table, so a re-added counter starts at 0."
                                loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.delete.a11y"
                                loc:Localize.TooltipKey="panel.counters.delete.tip">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets" Glyph="&#xE74D;" FontSize="11"
                                          Foreground="{StaticResource ErrBrush}" />
                                <TextBlock Text="DELETE COUNTER" Style="{StaticResource ToolStripLabelTextStyle}"
                                           loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.delete.label" />
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Button>

                    </StackPanel>
                </ScrollViewer>

                <!-- Empty state — a SIBLING of the scroller in the same cell,
                     never inside it. Two lines, no icon. -->
                <StackPanel Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.EmptyVisibility, Mode=OneWay}"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            Spacing="8">
                    <TextBlock Text="No counter selected"
                               FontFamily="{StaticResource DisplayFont}"
                               FontSize="20"
                               Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.empty.title" />
                    <TextBlock Text="Pick one from the list, or add a new counter."
                               FontFamily="{StaticResource SansFont}"
                               FontSize="12"
                               Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.empty.body" />
                </StackPanel>
            </Grid>

            <!-- ───────────── RIGHT 300 : the roster ───────────── -->
            <Border Grid.Column="1"
                    Background="{StaticResource CoalSurfaceBrush}"
                    BorderBrush="{StaticResource CoalCardBrush}"
                    BorderThickness="1,0,0,0">
                <Grid>
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- header       -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- column band  -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="*" />      <!-- roster       -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- source note  -->
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                    <!-- The one legal PanelHeader in the house shell: the right
                         column's own header. -->
                    <cmn:PanelHeader Grid.Row="0" Eyebrow="LIVE" Title="Counters"
                                     EyebrowKey="panel.common.eyebrow.live"
                                     TitleKey="panel.counters.roster.title">
                        <cmn:PanelHeader.RightContent>
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.RosterCountText, Mode=OneWay}"
                                       FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="11"
                                       Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </cmn:PanelHeader.RightContent>
                    </cmn:PanelHeader>

                    <Border Grid.Row="1"
                            Background="{StaticResource CoalRaisedBrush}"
                            BorderBrush="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="0,0,0,1"
                            Padding="14,6">
                        <Grid ColumnSpacing="8">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="26" />
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="#"
                                       FontFamily="{StaticResource SansFont}" FontSize="9" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       CharacterSpacing="140"
                                       Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="COUNTER"
                                       FontFamily="{StaticResource SansFont}" FontSize="9" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       CharacterSpacing="140"
                                       Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                                       loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roster.column.counter" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="!CMD"
                                       FontFamily="{StaticResource SansFont}" FontSize="9" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       CharacterSpacing="140"
                                       Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                                       loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roster.column.cmd" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Text="COUNT"
                                       FontFamily="{StaticResource SansFont}" FontSize="9" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       CharacterSpacing="140"
                                       Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                                       loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roster.column.count" />
                        </Grid>
                    </Border>

                    <Grid Grid.Row="2">
                        <ScrollViewer Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.RosterListVisibility, Mode=OneWay}"
                                      VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                                      HorizontalScrollMode="Disabled">
                            <!-- ItemsControl → ItemsRepeater. Nothing in this page's
                                 code-behind walks the visual tree for rows, so the
                                 swap is safe here; the row's own Click carries the
                                 selection (ItemsRepeater has no selection model). -->
                            <ItemsRepeater ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Counters, Mode=OneWay}"
                                           cmn:RowDataContext.Supply="True"
                                           AutomationProperties.Name="Counters, newest last"
                                           loc:Localize.AutomationKey="panel.counters.roster.list.a11y">
                                <ItemsRepeater.ItemTemplate>
                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="local:CounterRowVm">
                                        <Button Background="Transparent"
                                                BorderThickness="0"
                                                Padding="0"
                                                CornerRadius="0"
                                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                                HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch"
                                                Click="OnCounterRowClick"
                                                AutomationProperties.Name="{x:Bind NameEyebrow, Mode=OneWay}">
                                            <Grid Padding="14,7"
                                                  ColumnSpacing="8"
                                                  Background="{x:Bind RowBackground, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                  BorderBrush="{StaticResource CoalRaisedBrush}"
                                                  BorderThickness="0,0,0,1">
                                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="26" />
                                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                                                           Text="{x:Bind IndexText, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                           FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="11"
                                                           FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                           Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}" />
                                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                                                           Text="{x:Bind NameEyebrow, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                           FontFamily="{StaticResource SansFont}" FontSize="10"
                                                           FontWeight="SemiBold" CharacterSpacing="180"
                                                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                           Foreground="{StaticResource EmberPrimaryBrush}" />
                                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2"
                                                           Text="{x:Bind CommandBadgeText, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                           FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="11"
                                                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                           Foreground="{StaticResource Ember200Brush}" />
                                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="3"
                                                           Text="{x:Bind CountText, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                           FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}" FontSize="12"
                                                           FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                                           MinWidth="44"
                                                           TextAlignment="Right"
                                                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                           Foreground="{StaticResource CoalPrimaryTextBrush}" />
                                            </Grid>
                                        </Button>
                                    </DataTemplate>
                                </ItemsRepeater.ItemTemplate>
                            </ItemsRepeater>
                        </ScrollViewer>

                        <!-- ONE line, top-aligned, mono hint. Was two lines in
                             DisplayFont 20 floating in the vertical middle of a
                             tall empty column — a heading-sized announcement that
                             nothing exists yet. The column is 300 px now and the
                             sentence names the verb that fixes it. -->
                        <TextBlock Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.RosterEmptyVisibility, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Text="no counters yet &#xB7; + ADD COUNTER, top right"
                                   Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                   Padding="14,10"
                                   loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roster.empty" />
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Where the numbers actually live. Kept from the old body
                         hint; it belongs under the roster it describes — and
                         since the master-state banner went, this is the page's
                         one written statement that the open table keeps answering
                         db.* nodes while the tool is off. -->
                    <Border Grid.Row="3"
                            Background="{StaticResource CoalRaisedBrush}"
                            BorderBrush="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="0,1,0,0"
                            Padding="14,6">
                        <TextBlock Text="Counts live in the open Counters databank table, shared with the db.* nodes."
                                   Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}"
                                   loc:Localize.Key="panel.counters.roster.source_note" />
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
            </Border>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
